message.content:
Update the ZIP check API and the storefront widget to display cutoff time, delivery days, COD availability, and return policy. App at /Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Shopify App/Zip-Code.

IMPORTANT: The COD and return policy fields may not exist in the Prisma schema yet (another task is running that migration). Write the code to handle them gracefully — use optional chaining (`zipCode.codAvailable ?? null`) so it doesn't break if the field doesn't exist yet.

## Step 1: Read these files completely first
1. `app/routes/api.zip-check.tsx` — full file
2. `extensions/zip-code-widget/blocks/zip-code-checker.liquid` — full file
3. `app/routes/app.widget.tsx` — look for: DEFAULTS object, WidgetConfig shape, form fields for showEta/showZone/showWaitlistOnFailure toggles

---

## Step 2: Update api.zip-check.tsx

### Find the DeliveryRule matching logic
After finding the zip code, also query the matching DeliveryRule. The rule matches by zone (if the zip has a zone, find the active rule for that zone) or by specific zipCodes field. Read the current code to understand how/if delivery rules are already being queried.

If not currently queried, add:
```typescript
// Find best matching delivery rule
let deliveryRule = null;
if (zipRecord?.zone) {
  deliveryRule = await db.deliveryRule.findFirst({
    where: {
      shop,
      zone: zipRecord.zone,
      isActive: true,
    },
    orderBy: { priority: "asc" },
  });
}
```

### Include new fields in the JSON response
In the success/allowed response object, add:
```typescript
cutoffTime: deliveryRule?.cutoffTime ?? null,
daysOfWeek: deliveryRule?.daysOfWeek ?? null,
codAvailable: (zipRecord as any).codAvailable ?? null,  // will be typed after migration
returnPolicy: (zipRecord as any).returnPolicy ?? null,
```

Also include these in any "not found but default=allow" response path.

For blocked responses, still include codAvailable and returnPolicy from the zip record (merchants may want to show policies even for blocked zips — keep it simple, include them).

The full response shape should now be:
```typescript
{
  allowed: boolean,
  message: string,
  eta: string | null,
  zone: string | null,
  cutoffTime: string | null,      // NEW e.g. "14:00"
  daysOfWeek: string | null,      // NEW e.g. "Mon,Tue,Wed,Thu,Fri"
  codAvailable: boolean | null,   // NEW
  returnPolicy: string | null,    // NEW
  showWaitlist: boolean,
  notFound?: boolean,
}
```

---

## Step 3: Update the Liquid widget

Read the full liquid file. Find where the success result is rendered in JavaScript (where ETA and zone are displayed after a successful check). 

### Add cutoff time display
After the ETA display logic, add:
```javascript
// Cutoff time
if (result.cutoffTime) {
  var parts = result.cutoffTime.split(':');
  var hour = parseInt(parts[0], 10);
  var min = parts[1] || '00';
  var ampm = hour >= 12 ? 'PM' : 'AM';
  var h12 = hour % 12 || 12;
  var timeStr = h12 + ':' + min + ' ' + ampm;
  var cutEl = document.createElement('div');
  cutEl.className = 'zcc-cutoff';
  cutEl.textContent = '🕐 Order by ' + timeStr + ' for same-day delivery';
  successContainer.appendChild(cutEl);
}
```

### Add delivery days display
```javascript
// Delivery days
if (result.daysOfWeek) {
  var daysEl = document.createElement('div');
  daysEl.className = 'zcc-days';
  daysEl.textContent = '📅 Delivers: ' + result.daysOfWeek;
  successContainer.appendChild(daysEl);
}
```

### Add COD badge display
```javascript
// COD availability
if (result.codAvailable === true) {
  var codEl = document.createElement('div');
  codEl.className = 'zcc-cod zcc-cod--yes';
  codEl.textContent = '✓ Cash on Delivery Available';
  successContainer.appendChild(codEl);
} else if (result.codAvailable === false) {
  var codEl2 = document.createElement('div');
  codEl2.className = 'zcc-cod zcc-cod--no';
  codEl2.textContent = '✗ COD Not Available';
  successContainer.appendChild(codEl2);
}
```

### Add return policy display
```javascript
// Return policy
if (result.returnPolicy) {
  var rpEl = document.createElement('div');
  rpEl.className = 'zcc-return-policy';
  rpEl.textContent = '↩ ' + result.returnPolicy;
  successContainer.appendChild(rpEl);
}
```

IMPORTANT: Match the exact variable names used in the existing liquid for the success container element — read the file first to find the right variable name (it might be `successDiv`, `resultEl`, `container`, etc.).

### Add CSS for new elements
In the `<style>` section, add:
```css
.zcc-cutoff { margin-top: 6px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #6d7175; }
.zcc-days { margin-top: 4px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #6d7175; }
.zcc-cod { margin-top: 6px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; }
.zcc-cod--yes { color: #008060; }
.zcc-cod--no { color: #d72c0d; }
.zcc-return-policy { margin-top: 6px; font-size: 0.82em; color: #6d7175; border-top: 1px solid #e1e3e5; padding-top: 6px; margin-top: 8px; }
```

---

## Step 4: Update app.widget.tsx toggle controls

Read app/routes/app.widget.tsx. Find where showEta, showZone, showWaitlistOnFailure toggles are rendered. Add new toggles in the same pattern:

```tsx
<Checkbox
  label="Show cutoff time"
  helpText="Display order cutoff time for same-day delivery."
  checked={config.showCutoffTime ?? true}
  onChange={(v) => setConfig(c => ({ ...c, showCutoffTime: v }))}
/>
<Checkbox
  label="Show delivery days"
  helpText="Display which days of the week delivery is available."
  checked={config.showDeliveryDays ?? true}
  onChange={(v) => setConfig(c => ({ ...c, showDeliveryDays: v }))}
/>
<Checkbox
  label="Show COD availability"
  helpText="Display whether Cash on Delivery is available."
  checked={config.showCod ?? true}
  onChange={(v) => setConfig(c => ({ ...c, showCod: v }))}
/>
<Checkbox
  label="Show return policy"
  helpText="Display the return/exchange policy for the ZIP code."
  checked={config.showReturnPolicy ?? true}
  onChange={(v) => setConfig(c => ({ ...c, showReturnPolicy: v }))}
/>
```

Also update the DEFAULTS object to include these new boolean fields with `true` as default.

Update the widget config save action to persist these new fields to the DB (if the DB fields exist — use optional chaining or conditional inclusion).

---

## Final Step:
Run: `cd "/Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Shopify App/Zip-Code" && npm run typecheck`
Fix ALL TypeScript errors.

Read every file before changing. Use `(record as any).field` pattern for fields that may not be in the schema yet (the migration is running in parallel). TypeScript errors from missing Prisma fields can be suppressed with `as any` temporarily.

